{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01GPFoz2jbCzutxoKsJWshPw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q32 — Hallucination when retrieved context is irrelevant or absent**:\n\n**Core argument:** This is the most dangerous RAG failure because the LLM produces a *confident* wrong answer rather than flagging uncertainty. The fix is defense-in-depth across three layers:\n\n1. **Retrieval gate** (before the LLM call) — cosine similarity threshold (e.g. `< 0.70`) short-circuits the pipeline entirely, returning a canned abstention response. Saves LLM cost and prevents hallucination at the source.\n2. **Grounding prompt** (at generation) — explicit \"answer only from context, otherwise say you don't know\" instruction + temperature=0 + numbered citations. Forces the model to surface unsupported claims as visible gaps.\n3. **Post-generation faithfulness check** — async RAGAS `faithfulness` score; below 0.80 triggers flagging. NLI entailment (DeBERTa) for regulated domains. Semantic cache poisoning to suppress future similar queries.\n\n**Key pitfalls captured:** \"Temperature=0 fixes hallucination\" (wrong — it's a retrieval problem); running faithfulness inline as a real-time blocker (too slow — run async); conflating \"no docs returned\" with \"irrelevant docs returned\" (the second is more insidious).\n\n3 items remain in the Next queue (Q33, Q34, validate)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":381,"cache_read_input_tokens":61176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":381,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c96fceda-0284-4d3b-9635-2b74e1789ffd","uuid":"e270c339-8530-4877-80a0-d76fddfcc59d"}
